---
description: Project conventions (language, file headers, structure, Clerk orgs, database, secrets, styling, a11y). Full version in .claude/skills/project-conventions/SKILL.md
globs: src/**/*.ts,src/**/*.tsx,supabase/migrations/*.sql
alwaysApply: false
---

- All app text and code are in English: UI text, error messages, page titles, placeholders, code comments and SQL migration comments. The report and Jira stay in Danish.
- Every new or touched file in src/ starts with a 1–2 line /** */ comment saying what the file does (after 'use client' / 'use server').
- Files are kebab-case. Components use named exports; only files Next requires (page, layout, proxy …) use default export. Import with @/*. No barrel index.ts files.
- Keep a file in the route folder that uses it; move it to components/ or lib/ only when a second page needs it.
- When writing, reviewing or suggesting code, recommend a component when the same markup and classes appear 2+ times, or a block has its own state and makes its parent hard to read. Not for one-off markup. In code for the current task, make it. In existing code outside the task, only name the files and suggest a ticket.
- TypeScript strict: no any (use unknown + a type guard), type not interface, no enum (as const arrays).
- Server Components by default. With cacheComponents, per-request data and usePathname must render inside <Suspense>. Never fetch data in useEffect. Never use <img>.
- Get orgId on the server with await auth() in pages and server actions, or from the event payload in a webhook after its signature is verified (webhooks have no session, so no auth() there). Never from the browser, a URL or a form. Every query on customer data has WHERE auth_org_id = ${orgId}.
- All SQL goes through sql from @/lib/db as a tagged template. Never build SQL from strings. Server-side modules with secrets import 'server-only'.
- Database changes only as a new file in supabase/migrations/. Never edit an applied migration. Never run supabase db push without asking.
- Server actions re-check input and auth(), and return errors as data ({ ok: false, error }). Details go to console.error only. Webhooks verify the signature first.
- Secrets live in .env.local and Vercel env vars. Never prefix a secret with NEXT_PUBLIC_. Encrypt stored Shopify secrets with encrypt() from @/lib/crypto.
- Calls to Shopify and Photoroom go through their client in src/lib/<service>/.
- Tailwind utilities, mobile first, dark: variants. Put a repeated colour in @theme in globals.css instead of repeating the hex value.
- WCAG AA: semantic HTML, visible focus-visible/hover/disabled states, alt on every image, explain disabled buttons, aria-live for changing status.
- Run npm run lint and npm run build before saying you are done. No test runner.
